A multi-line documentation header with a `;` at the end of its first text
line. The comment ends there and the stranded header line does not parse,
so comment_text_after_terminator reports one error at the comment's `;`;
unexpected_token and undeclared_variable defer to it (issue #343).
-- input.ssl --
/*
 BuildSummary writes the nightly summary row;
 Parameters: dRunDate - the run date;
:PROCEDURE BuildSummary;
	:PARAMETERS dRunDate;
	:RETURN DateToString(dRunDate, "yyyyMMdd");
:ENDPROC;
-- format --
/*
 BuildSummary writes the nightly summary row;
Parameters:dRunDate - the run date;

:PROCEDURE BuildSummary;
	:PARAMETERS dRunDate;

	:RETURN DateToString(dRunDate, "yyyyMMdd");
:ENDPROC;
-- diagnostics --
2:45-2:46 error comment_text_after_terminator: The comment ends at this ';', so the next line, starting 'Parameters', is parsed as code. It reads as a stranded comment line; remove the ';' from the comment text
-- diagnostics [--strict --info] --
2:45-2:46 error comment_text_after_terminator: The comment ends at this ';', so the next line, starting 'Parameters', is parsed as code. It reads as a stranded comment line; remove the ';' from the comment text
